WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:04.070
Just moments ago, Chinese leader Xi
Jinping arrived in Moscow for a three day

00:00:04.070 --> 00:00:04.804
state visit.

00:00:04.804 --> 00:00:08.375
This is his first visit to Russia
since Russia invaded Ukraine.

00:00:08.375 --> 00:00:11.611
And later this morning, he will hold a one
on one meeting with Vladimir Putin.

00:00:11.878 --> 00:00:16.116
This is Western leaders grow very weary
of the two nations deepening cooperation.

00:00:16.149 --> 00:00:18.752
Ivan Watson joins us live from Kiev,
Ukraine.

00:00:18.752 --> 00:00:21.121
Ivan,
thank you very much for being with us.

00:00:21.454 --> 00:00:23.056
This is such a significant meeting

00:00:23.056 --> 00:00:26.359
and it comes
just on the heels of President Putin

00:00:26.626 --> 00:00:31.164
going to Mariupol right after he visited
Crimea and Rostov on.

00:00:32.098 --> 00:00:34.801
There is so much at stake here.

00:00:34.801 --> 00:00:38.138
And the West obviously very concerned,
even though China is feeling

00:00:38.138 --> 00:00:41.441
this as a mission of peace.

00:00:42.442 --> 00:00:42.742
Right.

00:00:42.742 --> 00:00:44.744
And the Ukrainians
watching this very nervously.

00:00:44.911 --> 00:00:48.181
And that's because Xi
Jinping and Vladimir Putin,

00:00:48.415 --> 00:00:51.251
they keep talking about their friendship
with no limits.

00:00:51.251 --> 00:00:56.089
This incredible basically alliance
between Russia and China.

00:00:56.356 --> 00:00:59.592
Xi Jinping sent a letter
to Russian state media before this trip.

00:00:59.793 --> 00:01:03.730
He says this is the 10th time he's
visiting Russia since he became president.

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:07.534
It'll be his 40th meeting
with Vladimir Putin.

00:01:07.734 --> 00:01:11.704
He had some digs in his letter,
thinly veiled at the U.S.

00:01:11.704 --> 00:01:17.177
complaining about hegemony and and calling
for a more democratic, multipolar world.

00:01:17.444 --> 00:01:20.180
What he did not mention at all
was Russia's

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:23.850
invasion of Ukraine a year ago
and the ongoing war.

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:30.256
Instead, Xi Jinping referred to this
as the Ukraine crisis and claimed that

00:01:30.256 --> 00:01:34.194
Beijing is neutral in this,
that he wants peace

00:01:34.194 --> 00:01:37.063
negotiations and dialog.

00:01:37.630 --> 00:01:41.367
He has yet to speak directly
with the Ukrainian

00:01:41.401 --> 00:01:45.572
president, Volodymyr Zelensky,
since Russia's invasion a year ago.

00:01:45.772 --> 00:01:49.742
And when it comes to the International
Criminal Court issuing an arrest warrant

00:01:49.742 --> 00:01:53.847
on Friday against Vladimir Putin
for alleged war crimes.

00:01:54.147 --> 00:01:56.649
Well, the Chinese Foreign Ministry
has weighed in on that.

00:01:57.083 --> 00:02:01.454
It is calling for the ICC
to be objective and impartial.

00:02:01.454 --> 00:02:05.892
Rule to respect the jurisdictional
immunity enjoyed by a head of state

00:02:06.159 --> 00:02:09.762
and to avoid politicization
and double standards.

00:02:10.196 --> 00:02:15.869
So take that into context when you discuss

00:02:16.136 --> 00:02:18.872
China's claimed neutrality in this war.

00:02:19.005 --> 00:02:21.307
And China has at no point

00:02:21.307 --> 00:02:25.211
throughout this war
it condemned Russia's invasion of Ukraine.

00:02:25.245 --> 00:02:29.616
They remain a huge buyer of Russian
oil helping finance all of this.

00:02:29.883 --> 00:02:33.052
And one of the things that the West,
John Kirby here

00:02:33.586 --> 00:02:36.122
in the US and the White House
has been warning against is

00:02:36.122 --> 00:02:39.592
if China were to come out
after this visit, Ivan and

00:02:40.627 --> 00:02:42.262
say, well, there should be a

00:02:42.262 --> 00:02:47.033
peace deal right now
that would not be palatable by Ukraine

00:02:47.033 --> 00:02:49.802
in the West,
given that Russia has taken more territory

00:02:50.170 --> 00:02:53.106
than when this all began.

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:54.841
Sure.

00:02:54.841 --> 00:02:57.844
And has declared that it is annexing
Ukrainian

00:02:57.844 --> 00:03:01.814
territory seized
since the invasion of last year.

00:03:01.814 --> 00:03:05.652
And to underscore that you had Vladimir
Putin on Saturday,

00:03:05.652 --> 00:03:12.025
fresh from this ICC arrest warrant,
visiting the Russian occupied Ukrainian

00:03:12.025 --> 00:03:15.528
city of Mariupol, all the Kremlin says
he landed by helicopter.

00:03:15.662 --> 00:03:19.566
He drove himself into the outskirts
of that shattered city

00:03:19.799 --> 00:03:22.602
and visited an apartment building
that the Russian government

00:03:22.602 --> 00:03:25.872
just built while he's meeting with
some of the residents there Poppy.

00:03:26.139 --> 00:03:28.775
You hear a voice off camera
that our linguists say

00:03:29.309 --> 00:03:31.110
somebody was yelling, this is all a show.

00:03:31.110 --> 00:03:32.946
It's not true.

00:03:32.946 --> 00:03:36.950
This time last year,
the Russian military had encircled

00:03:36.950 --> 00:03:42.088
that city and was bombing it from land,
sea and air, destroying much of it.

00:03:42.255 --> 00:03:45.858
And I was interviewing residents
who were fleeing, who described

00:03:45.858 --> 00:03:49.963
spending weeks under bombardment,
terrified, hiding in basements,

00:03:50.296 --> 00:03:53.333
burying neighbors
who got killed by Russian

00:03:53.333 --> 00:03:56.302
artillery in the front yards
of their apartment buildings.

00:03:56.502 --> 00:03:59.305
And I spoke to one of the women
I met a year ago who escaped.

00:03:59.539 --> 00:04:01.741
She's living she's a refugee overseas.

00:04:01.941 --> 00:04:05.311
She said seeing Vladimir
Putin in her hometown

00:04:05.578 --> 00:04:09.983
is like seeing a serial killer
return to the scene of the crime.

00:04:10.483 --> 00:04:11.851
Yeah, of course it is.

00:04:11.851 --> 00:04:13.253
And that really says it all.

00:04:13.253 --> 00:04:16.356
Ivan Watson,
thank you for the reporting from Kiev.

00:04:16.623 --> 00:04:19.959
Talk to us about what you expect
from these three days, given the fact

00:04:19.959 --> 00:04:24.797
that China that Xi Jinping just said
moments ago reiterated his willingness

00:04:25.365 --> 00:04:29.802
to work with Vladimir Putin to, quote,
safeguard the international order.

00:04:29.802 --> 00:04:34.007
This is after Putin
just before invading Ukraine,

00:04:34.007 --> 00:04:38.478
talked about their relationship, these two
leaders, as a no limits partnership

00:04:41.648 --> 00:04:42.115
That's right.

00:04:42.115 --> 00:04:44.350
I worry about two different things here.

00:04:44.384 --> 00:04:48.388
The first I've raised before,
which is do we see arms?

00:04:48.388 --> 00:04:52.925
And, you know, basically we see
the Chinese getting further into this war.

00:04:53.426 --> 00:04:56.162
Think the second thing to look for
is whether or not

00:04:56.162 --> 00:05:00.700
in some kind of peace
proposal for an armistice or a cease fire,

00:05:01.768 --> 00:05:05.371
essentially the Chinese
come in on the side of the Russians

00:05:05.672 --> 00:05:08.641
to try to cement
the gains that they have right now.

00:05:09.042 --> 00:05:12.245
And that's why you're hearing
from the Americans

00:05:12.245 --> 00:05:16.983
and from President Stilinski
and Ukrainians, great concern

00:05:17.417 --> 00:05:19.886
that China would seek in some way

00:05:20.119 --> 00:05:25.425
to reward Russia and basically freeze
this the way the Korean conflict

00:05:25.425 --> 00:05:28.261
has been frozen now for 50 or 60 years.

00:05:30.263 --> 00:05:33.333
This seems to be
what they're really worried about the US

00:05:33.466 --> 00:05:37.170
in terms of trying to preempt John Kirby,
who's going to come on the program

00:05:37.170 --> 00:05:40.840
a little later today, has been saying
it would not be acceptable.

00:05:40.873 --> 00:05:42.675
So China is trying
to play this peacemaker,

00:05:42.675 --> 00:05:45.545
but it would not be acceptable for China
to come out and say,

00:05:45.812 --> 00:05:49.115
okay, let's push towards peace right now
in this moment.

00:05:49.515 --> 00:05:52.919
Because in this moment,
Russia has taken more

00:05:52.919 --> 00:05:57.023
Ukrainian territory
than obviously before the invasion

00:05:59.459 --> 00:06:00.126
That's right.

00:06:00.126 --> 00:06:03.196
And that's a significant worry.

00:06:03.663 --> 00:06:07.033
On the other hand, the trends have to be
a little bit cautious here,

00:06:07.433 --> 00:06:10.069
and they have to be cautious
because they're worried about Europe.

00:06:10.503 --> 00:06:13.773
They would like to make sure
that Europe does not join

00:06:14.073 --> 00:06:17.910
in any sanctions against China,
that they that Europe

00:06:17.910 --> 00:06:22.148
and the United States do not tighten
this bond that has been created

00:06:22.148 --> 00:06:25.284
since the the war began.

00:06:25.685 --> 00:06:28.621
And, you know, Europe's
a major trading partner for them

00:06:28.621 --> 00:06:31.557
and is continuing
to take a good deal of their technology.

00:06:31.924 --> 00:06:34.994
So I think they're not going
to want to get in too deep.

00:06:35.495 --> 00:06:38.965
And that's one reason I think, that
they've probably been cautious so far

00:06:39.198 --> 00:06:41.567
in providing weapons to the Russians.

00:06:42.034 --> 00:06:45.438
The problem is the Russians don't have
very many other places to turn right now.

00:06:45.471 --> 00:06:48.541
Their only other sources are Iran
and North Korea.

00:06:48.808 --> 00:06:52.578
And obviously, the quality of that is
not up to what China could give them.

00:06:53.546 --> 00:06:56.449
Also, David, what it says about China
on the world stage,

00:06:56.449 --> 00:06:59.118
because this comes after China
just brokered

00:06:59.886 --> 00:07:02.355
a diplomatic deal
with Iran and Saudi Arabia.

00:07:02.588 --> 00:07:06.225
Now we're seeing them try
to assert themselves in this way, saying,

00:07:06.225 --> 00:07:09.962
you know, they are this powerful influence
when it comes to international order.

00:07:12.165 --> 00:07:14.300
They would love nothing more, Caitlin,

00:07:14.367 --> 00:07:17.570
than to play the role
that the United States played during

00:07:17.570 --> 00:07:20.506
much of the Cold War in post-Cold
War period,

00:07:20.840 --> 00:07:24.577
which is the central player
that everybody had to come to

00:07:24.577 --> 00:07:29.048
so that they could organize the world
on the basis of the rules

00:07:29.348 --> 00:07:33.553
that they consider advantageous
And they think the United States did this

00:07:33.553 --> 00:07:38.891
from the end of World War Two in 1945
through to just a few years ago.

00:07:39.158 --> 00:07:41.027
And that's why
it was so important to them.

00:07:41.027 --> 00:07:43.830
To play this role between Iran and Saudi
Arabia

00:07:44.130 --> 00:07:46.599
and would be important
to them to do this now.

00:07:47.066 --> 00:07:50.403
And of course, the United States
not only doesn't want to give up

00:07:50.403 --> 00:07:53.973
its position on that,
but it also is suspicious

00:07:54.273 --> 00:07:57.710
that China is not the neutral player
that it pretends to be.

00:07:57.743 --> 00:08:00.713
Of course, that's what
the Chinese say about the United States.

00:08:01.080 --> 00:08:01.447
All of it.

00:08:01.447 --> 00:08:03.816
And very interesting optics
for Vladimir Putin,

00:08:03.816 --> 00:08:07.019
especially after just visiting Mariupol,
I going to the war zone.

00:08:07.053 --> 00:08:08.588
David, what do you make of that?

00:08:10.022 --> 00:08:10.790
It is

00:08:10.790 --> 00:08:13.526
I mean, he was doing two
or three things there, Don.

00:08:13.893 --> 00:08:17.296
The first is he wanted to say,
this is my territory now.

00:08:17.797 --> 00:08:23.302
You know, this is an area that obviously
they not only bombed and destroyed,

00:08:23.503 --> 00:08:27.473
but it's an area where they kidnaped
many of those children for whom

00:08:28.307 --> 00:08:31.110
he was indicted
by the International Criminal Court.

00:08:31.444 --> 00:08:35.414
Because second thing he was saying
was the indictment means nothing to me,

00:08:35.414 --> 00:08:36.482
in fact.

00:08:36.682 --> 00:08:39.852
They'll continue
with all of their activities in Mariupol.

00:08:39.852 --> 00:08:41.921
That they have done until now.

00:08:42.255 --> 00:08:44.257
So it was a real act of defiance.

00:08:44.590 --> 00:08:49.695
And clearly getting into the endorsement
of having Xi Jinping show up

00:08:50.096 --> 00:08:52.231
for their 39th meeting

00:08:53.466 --> 00:08:55.535
since the two of them took over
as leaders.

00:08:55.535 --> 00:08:57.770
That's pretty significant.

00:08:57.970 --> 00:08:59.906
All right. David Sanger.
Always a pleasure.

00:08:59.906 --> 00:09:01.140
Good to see you. Thank you so much.

